{"requirements":[{"id":"log-forwarding-and-persistence","requirement":"Forward node2 inventory application messages to node1 and persist them at /var/log/inventory/node2.log.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A post-restart inventory message emitted on node2 was received in the required file on node1. The final check also showed earlier persisted messages and confirmed that a differently tagged application message was excluded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3cd5c14210344e81","cmd-11ba5b3969434a4e"]},{"id":"node1-restart-recovery","requirement":"Keep log flow and stored data working after node1 restarts.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Evidence captures a healthy pre-restart collector, acknowledged restart, changed boot identity, collector unavailability during the bounded outage, and full recovery. An inventory message emitted while node1 was unavailable was delivered afterward, while pre-restart data remained present.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8f11dd2a02ab4000","cmd-fca1005241544952","cmd-2091cb89e73d4998","cmd-0f152be8d86244af","cmd-eabf28dd0b7a45b0","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"node2-restart-recovery","requirement":"Keep log flow working after node2 restarts.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The sender had a healthy pre-restart connection and successful delivery, the restart was acknowledged, its boot identity changed, rsyslog and the forwarding configuration recovered, the TCP session re-established, and a fresh inventory message reached node1.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b858907b18be4673","cmd-ed7f365f2cf54a9c","cmd-2dd37332e6ba4337","cmd-5f7cb0ae408148fc","cmd-3cd5c14210344e81","cmd-11ba5b3969434a4e","global:before_prepare:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity"]},{"id":"legacy-platform-preservation","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use legacy-platform-compatible software.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 7.9 with kernel 3.10.0-1160.el7.x86_64. The existing packaged rsyslog 8.24 configuration validated and operated successfully after both restarts.","evidence_ids":["global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:before_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","cmd-359f654dc0aa40da","cmd-11ba5b3969434a4e"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"Task-related configuration, firewall, service restarts, test messages, and node restarts all had clear causal roles. The only unwanted residue was one reboot-helper log left in /tmp on each node; these remained after execution rather than being cleaned up. They originated from the asynchronous restart commands in cmd-fca1005241544952 and cmd-2dd37332e6ba4337. The initial unprivileged setup attempt showed errors and provides no evidence of mutation. No failed services or other harmful residue was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fca1005241544952","cmd-2dd37332e6ba4337","cmd-e9f2897ca7514e76","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. Inventory-only forwarding and persistence were directly demonstrated, and bounded restart tests on both managed nodes showed changed boot identities and restored end-to-end operation. The required RHEL release and kernel were preserved. Provider-wide restart evidence is complete and agrees with the fixed lifecycle boot-identity observations.","limitations":["Package-manager consistency checks timed out in both lifecycle snapshots, so package health beyond the directly observed unchanged platform and functioning packaged rsyslog is not independently established.","The lifecycle snapshots are bounded inventories; task-specific files and persisted log contents rely on the executor's direct command evidence."]}
